{"info":{"author":"AI Verify","author_email":null,"bugtrack_url":null,"classifiers":["Development Status :: 4 - Beta","License :: OSI Approved :: Apache Software License","Programming Language :: Python :: 3","Programming Language :: Python :: 3.10","Programming Language :: Python :: 3.11"],"description":"# AI Verify Test Engine\n\n## Description\n\nAI Verify Test Engine provides core interfaces, converters, data, model and plugin managers to facilitate the development of tests for AI systems. It is used as a base library for all AI Verify official stock-plugins and can be used to develop custom plugins.\n\n## Installation\n\nInstall `aiverify-test-engine` via pip. The following table list the available install options and the optional dependencies along with the additional functionality that is supported.\n\n| Installation Command                           | Description                                                                                                                                        |\n| ---------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `pip install aiverify-test-engine`             | Installs only the core functionalites. Supports tabular data formats like CSV, as well as Pandas pickle and Joblib files, and Scikit-learn models. |\n| `pip install aiverify-test-engine[dev]`        | Includes additional dependencies for development. Intended for developers who want to contribute to the project.                                   |\n| `pip install aiverify-test-engine[tensorflow]` | Installs optional Tensorflow and Keras dependencies.                                                                                               |\n| `pip install aiverify-test-engine[pytorch]`    | Installs optional PyTorch dependencies.                                                                                                            |\n| `pip install aiverify-test-engine[gbm]`        | Installs XGBoost and LightGBM packages. Supports serializing models in these formats.                                                              |\n| `pip install aiverify-test-engine[all]`        | Installs the core package along with all additional non development dependencies.                                                                  |\n\n## Developer Guide\n\n### Local Installation\n\nTo contribute changes to the test engine code, clone the repository, navigate to the `aiverify-test-engine` folder, and install the dev version of the library:\n\n```bash\npip install '.[dev]'\n```\n\nHere's an overview of the project folder structure and a brief description of each:\n\n```bash\naiverify-test-engine/\n├── aiverify_test_engine/   # Core library code\n│   ├── interfaces/         # Core interfaces (algorithm, converter, data, model, pipeline, serializer, plugin)\n│   ├── io/                 # Data and model IO related logic\n│   ├── plugins/            # Manage the loading and execution of algorithm, data, model, pipeline and plugins\n│   ├── utils/              # Utility functions and validators\n├── tests/                  # Test cases\n├── pyproject.toml          # Project configuration file\n```\n\n### Running Tests\n\n```bash\npython -m pytest tests\n```\n\nIf Tensorflow has trouble with GPU, use following environment variable to force Tensorflow to use CPU:\n```bash\nCUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=\"\" TF_CPP_MIN_LOG_LEVEL=2 TF_NUM_INTEROP_THREADS=1 TF_NUM_INTRAOP_THREADS=1 XLA_FLAGS=\"--xla_gpu_unsafe_fallback_to_driver_on_ptxas_not_found\" python -m pytest tests\n```\n\n### Building the Package\n\n```bash\nhatch build\n```\n\n## License\n\n- Licensed under Apache Software License 2.0\n\n## Developers:\n\n- AI Verify\n","description_content_type":"text/markdown","docs_url":null,"download_url":null,"downloads":{"last_day":-1,"last_month":-1,"last_week":-1},"dynamic":null,"home_page":null,"keywords":null,"license":"Apache Software License 2.0","license_expression":null,"license_files":["AUTHORS.rst","LICENSE","NOTICE.md"],"maintainer":null,"maintainer_email":null,"name":"aiverify-test-engine","package_url":"https://pypi.org/project/aiverify-test-engine/","platform":null,"project_url":"https://pypi.org/project/aiverify-test-engine/","project_urls":null,"provides_extra":["all","dev","gbm","pytorch","tensorflow"],"release_url":"https://pypi.org/project/aiverify-test-engine/2.2.1/","requires_dist":["aiometer==0.5.0","async-timeout==4.0.3","attrs==23.2.0","joblib==1.4.2","jsonschema-specifications~=2024.10.1","jsonschema~=4.24","libclang==16.0.6","numpy==1.26.4","openapi-schema-validator~=0.7.3","pandas==2.2.2","pydantic==2.*","referencing~=0.37.0","requests>=2.32.4","rpds-py~=0.25.1","scikit-learn==1.5.2","scipy==1.14.1","setuptools>=78.1.1","urllib3>=2.6.3","keras>=3.12.1; extra == \"all\"","lightgbm>=4.6.0; extra == \"all\"","protobuf>=6.33.5; extra == \"all\"","tensorflow>=2.18.0; extra == \"all\"","torch>=2.10; extra == \"all\"","torchvision>=0.15.0; extra == \"all\"","werkzeug>=3.1.6; extra == \"all\"","xgboost==2.1.1; extra == \"all\"","anybadge==1.14.0; extra == \"dev\"","coverage==7.3.2; extra == \"dev\"","hatch==1.12.0; extra == \"dev\"","jaraco-context>=6.1.0; extra == \"dev\"","keras>=3.12.1; extra == \"dev\"","lightgbm>=4.6.0; extra == \"dev\"","pillow>=12.1.1; extra == \"dev\"","pre-commit==3.5.0; extra == \"dev\"","protobuf>=6.33.5; extra == \"dev\"","pytest-cov==5.0.0; extra == \"dev\"","pytest-html==4.1.1; extra == \"dev\"","pytest-json-report==1.5.0; extra == \"dev\"","pytest-json==0.4.0; extra == \"dev\"","pytest-mock==3.12.0; extra == \"dev\"","pytest==7.4.3; extra == \"dev\"","ruff==0.7.1; extra == \"dev\"","tensorflow>=2.18.0; extra == \"dev\"","torch>=2.10; extra == \"dev\"","torchvision>=0.15.0; extra == \"dev\"","uv>=0.9.6; extra == \"dev\"","werkzeug>=3.1.6; extra == \"dev\"","xgboost==2.1.1; extra == \"dev\"","lightgbm>=4.6.0; extra == \"gbm\"","xgboost==2.1.1; extra == \"gbm\"","torch>=2.10; extra == \"pytorch\"","torchvision>=0.15.0; extra == \"pytorch\"","keras>=3.12.1; extra == \"tensorflow\"","protobuf>=6.33.5; extra == \"tensorflow\"","tensorflow>=2.18.0; extra == \"tensorflow\"","werkzeug>=3.1.6; extra == \"tensorflow\""],"requires_python":"<3.13,>=3.10","summary":"AI Verify Test Engine provides core interfaces, converters, data, model and plugin managers to facilitate the development of tests for AI systems. It is used as a base library for all AI Verify official stock-plugins and can be used to develop custom plugins.","version":"2.2.1","yanked":false,"yanked_reason":null},"last_serial":35320642,"ownership":{"organization":null,"roles":[{"role":"Owner","user":"aiverify-foundation"}]},"releases":{"2.0.0":[{"comment_text":null,"core-metadata":{"sha256":"01b8edca1442736eb67a8524e426fced588a2aa60920c9cdcbff2edb1cadb1f5"},"digests":{"blake2b_256":"8f8278d051f8e2bd2165f654b365f5e32c54fbac3cf749e82b81d441d89aee13","md5":"933a5ed66e9308777e43d2966fe79e30","sha256":"7517e9ef5d5a12f9af8ea2a45c67290a850ac2de518aeb8ca312a73fb487ba1b"},"downloads":-1,"filename":"aiverify_test_engine-2.0.0-py3-none-any.whl","has_sig":false,"md5_digest":"933a5ed66e9308777e43d2966fe79e30","packagetype":"bdist_wheel","python_version":"py3","requires_python":"<3.12,>=3.10","size":85809,"upload_time":"2025-04-17T08:49:23","upload_time_iso_8601":"2025-04-17T08:49:23.650962Z","url":"https://files.pythonhosted.org/packages/8f/82/78d051f8e2bd2165f654b365f5e32c54fbac3cf749e82b81d441d89aee13/aiverify_test_engine-2.0.0-py3-none-any.whl","yanked":false,"yanked_reason":null},{"comment_text":null,"core-metadata":false,"digests":{"blake2b_256":"8f6c2dd956e58fa4efe482e1a0c9e16b2b97bca47f437c7f787dc8afc623a79a","md5":"25d4dd27cf18f0dc569bfb8740faf2a0","sha256":"459fea3a377a9f20a14aa93ce5e2c29490738c221c01841e631bdc44d5d041d2"},"downloads":-1,"filename":"aiverify_test_engine-2.0.0.tar.gz","has_sig":false,"md5_digest":"25d4dd27c